## Task G1 — App-server owner self-reexec path (split of original G)

Derived from: I010 + I011. Split of original P2.M2.E1.T004 (G) per D
(`.collab/research/2026-07-20T01-10-09Z-i011-process-model-and-disruption.md`):
app-server owner self-reexec is a materially different owner from outer-loop
inner/sidecar cycling and must not share one implementation.

Depends on E + F. Sister task: G2 (outer-loop adapters) under the same epic.

### Scope
Finalize the **Codex app-server** restart-stale path against the generic
owner-control seam (F) and the idle capability contract (E):

1. Ensure `restart-stale` continues to drive app-server instances via owner-control
   request/result (already shipped by I010 / P2.M1), not via generic `c2c restart`
   TTY-capturing exec.
2. Consume E's typed Idle|Busy|Unknown for app-server: default auto only on
   authoritative Idle; Busy/Unknown fail closed to skip/guided unless `--force`.
3. Preserve same-pane owner PID continuity, exact thread resume, controlled env,
   and B098 (local operator only).
4. Unit/hermetic coverage for idle/force policy on the app-server path; do not
   re-run the full live deploy gate unless behaviour regresses.

### Out of scope
- Claude / OpenCode / Kimi / agy / Codex(hooks) adapters — those are G2.
- Spike work (H/I/J) and final docs closeout (K).

### Acceptance criteria
- App-server managed instances: default auto-restart only on authoritative Idle;
  Busy/Unknown fail closed; `--force` drives owner-control restart in-pane.
- No TTY theft; no ambient-env leak; B098 preserved.
- Hermetic tests cover the idle/force policy boundary for app-server.
- Does NOT alone close I010's all-managed-instance AC — G2 must also ship.

### Original G AC closure (shared with G2)
Together with G2, G1 restores the original G acceptance: by default the command
safely classifies/handles every stale target (auto on authoritative Idle;
guided otherwise); `restart-stale --force` restarts every current managed client
in-pane.


### Split provenance (2026-07-20)
Original single task G (P2.M2.E1.T004) was split before claim per D's determination
into G1 (this task, app-server) and G2 (P2.M2.E1.T005, outer-loop). Original
dependency/acceptance closure is preserved across G1+G2; K depends on both.